+    "content": "# Joint link-matter Hamiltonian: conditional theorem v0.1\n\nStatus: DERIVED conditional finite mathematics under a CANDIDATE action. Constructor verification only; independent review pending. Physical promotion 0.\n\nOn the 15-node, 28-link tetrahedral Hasse graph, put a unitary U(r) link and a Hermitian electric momentum on every adjacent incidence pair. Add two independent canonical complex matter fields at every node, transforming in fundamental and conjugate representations. The extra species, phase space, electric energy and Wilson-type diamond potential are explicit modeling inputs, not source-derived physics.\n\nThe chosen Hamiltonian has a canonical moment map\n\n    G_i = sum_head E - sum_tail U^dagger E U - psi_i psi_i^dagger + bar(chi_i) chi_i^T.\n\nThese matrix Gauss constraints are first class and preserved. Reciprocal matter force is derived from the same Hamiltonian that transports the matter. H, N_psi and N_chi are conserved. Unit links, conserved norms and the degree-four energy bound give unique global temporal-gauge flow for a>0, kappa>=0, mu>=0.\n\nA scoped obstruction appears before the repair: with only the canonical fundamental species, closed full-U(r) Gauss law and no external charges, summing its trace forces N_psi=0. This does not exclude SU(r), alternative matter phase spaces, boundaries or added sources. The selected two-species model admits arbitrary nonzero psi, chi=bar(psi), E=0 and arbitrary unitary links as neutral initial data. This is an initial preparation, not generally an invariant relation.\n\nThe neutral scalar seed psi=chi, each equal to one at vertex {0} and edge {0,1} and zero elsewhere, starts with identity links and zero electric momentum. Its selected link has E_dot=4. Two diamond phases acquire absolute second derivative 4a. With positive curl orientation,\n\n    phi(s) = 2 a s^2 + O(s^3),\n    1-cos(phi(s)) = 2 a^2 s^4 + O(s^5).\n\nThe defect's fourth derivative is 48 a^2. Thus the declared joint dynamics can generate spatial curvature from flat, Gauss-admissible initial data without external injection. The prior flat-connection and fixed-operator theorems retain their hypotheses and conclusions.\n\nVerification: 28 exact constructor checks plus a separately typed full-graph scalar numerical cross-check. Written universal proofs accompany finite fixtures. No experimental dataset was used. Standard canonical lattice gauge dynamics is credited; no general novelty claim is made.\n\nOpen gates: action and matter selection from UD; independent review; physical rank/algebra and representations; gauge-reduced modes and stability; continuum/relativistic behavior; quantum/chiral matter; units; kinetic normalization and renormalization-group matching; proton operators; monopole topology and physical data correspondence. This milestone supplies no force-unification proof, proton lifetime or monopole prediction.\n\nRecommended next step: analyze admissible neutral stationary backgrounds, remove gauge directions and derive the coupled linearized spectrum and stability conditions. Recommendation score 97/100 measures anticipated research value, not closure percentage or probability of physical correctness.\n"
