+Replay: `python3 verify_joint_hamiltonian.py` (Python 3, SymPy, NumPy, SciPy). It writes separate exact and numerical receipts. The verifier is authored by the constructor; it is not independent review.
+
+Build PDF: run `pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error UD_JOINT_HAMILTONIAN_THEOREM_v0.1.tex` twice. The source requires standard AMS, Latin Modern, geometry, hyperref, microtype, enumitem and fancyhdr packages.
+
+Claims and action assumptions are machine-readable in CLAIM_AND_BRIDGE_LEDGER_v0.1.json and HAMILTONIAN_CONTRACT_v0.1.json. SOURCE_PROVENANCE_v0.1.json distinguishes inherited graph inputs from declared additions and primary background sources. No experimental data were analyzed. The source-selected action, physical group, representations, continuum and physical correspondence remain open.
+
+The previous gauge-transport release and existing source papers remain frozen. This release is an additive conditional dynamics branch.
